      },
      "message": "fix(post): a flipped Z refusal names the exact reason\n\nA flipped WCS Z stays refused at the verification gate and in the post engine. The refusal now names why: on a control that reads Z reversed, the tool-length word (G43 or G44) depends on how the tool lengths were measured, and the project does not state it. A section with a canned cycle also names the R plane. Both doors read post::wcs_flip::Z_REASON. The decision is in docs/decisions/2474-wcs-flip-z-refusal.md.\n\nFixes #2474\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
